# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECRETS — never commit these
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .env.local holds the Supabase SERVICE ROLE key, the R2 secret access
# key, the Razorpay secret and the VAPID private key. The service role
# key bypasses row-level security entirely — anyone with it can read and
# write every shop's records. Committing it to a public repo means
# rotating all of them, immediately.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Service-account and key material, whatever it is called
*.pem
*.key
*-service-account*.json
credentials.json

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CUSTOMER DATA — real people's records
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The migration script writes a CSV of skipped rows to the working
# directory. It contains customer names and loan numbers.
migration-issues-*.csv

# Data exports produced by /api/export
*-export-*.zip
loanpro-*.zip

# A copy of a customer's desktop database, if one is restored locally
# for a dry run
*.loanprobackup
*.sql.gz
dump.sql

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Dependencies and build output
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/releases

/.next/
/out/
/build
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vercel
.vercel

# Supabase local development
supabase/.branches
supabase/.temp
supabase/.env

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Testing and logs
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
/coverage
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Editors and operating systems
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Deliberately NOT ignored
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# package-lock.json is committed on purpose. It is what guarantees the
# team and CI install identical versions — and a missing or stale
# lockfile is exactly what caused this project to install Next 9
# against a package.json asking for Next 15.
